"""Present the exact four-copy PPT exclusion at fifteen qubits."""
from pathlib import Path
import html,json,re,hashlib
HERE=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;ROOT=HERE.parents[1]
def m(x,display=True):
 tag='div' if display else 'span';return f'<{tag} class="math" data-display="{str(display).lower()}" data-tex="{html.escape(x,quote=True)}"></{tag}>'
def links(items):return '<div class="proof-links">'+''.join(f'<a href="{html.escape(u,quote=True)}">{t} ↗</a>' for u,t in items)+'</div>'
def main():
 r=json.loads((HERE/'independent-verification.json').read_text());assert r['passed']
 sha=hashlib.sha256((HERE/'certificate.json').read_bytes()).hexdigest();assert sha in [r.get('certificateSHA256'),r.get('sourceSHA256')]
 css=re.search(r'<style>(.*?)</style>',(ROOT/'research/t2-qec-upper/index.html').read_text(),re.S).group(1)
 css+='\n.math{max-width:100%;overflow-x:auto}.proof-step{border-left:3px solid #b8c9bd;padding-left:1.2rem;margin:2rem 0}.badge{color:#1c6253;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.08em}'
 b='<p class="eyebrow">Anticoherent states and subspaces · Exact exclusion</p><a href="../../index.html#n=15&t=4">← Catalogue entry</a><h1>Fifteen qubits cannot be fourth-order anticoherent</h1>'
 b+='<div class="result"><span class="badge">Proved · arbitrary complex pure states</span>'+m(r'\boxed{K(15,t)=0\quad(t\ge4),\qquad t_{\max}(15)=3.}')+'<p>A four-copy moment and its partial transpose must both be positive. An exact rational certificate shows that these positivity conditions contradict fourth-order anticoherence. No constellation symmetry or restricted Dicke support is assumed.</p></div>'
 b+='<section><h2>The complete answer at orders two, three and four</h2>'+m(r'\boxed{\bigl(K(15,2),K(15,3),K(15,4)\bigr)=(3,1,0).}')+'<p>The existing exact algebraic three-dimensional AC2 subspace is optimal. A separate four-copy certificate excludes every AC3 plane, and a four-component Dicke-basis superposition attains order three. The present proof excludes order four, and hence every higher order.</p>'+links([('../n15-t3/index.html#second-order','Second-order construction and upper bound'),('../n15-t3/index.html','Third-order maximum and explicit state')])+'</section>'
 b+='<section><h2>The exclusion argument</h2><div class="proof-step"><h3>1. Form a positive four-copy moment</h3><p>For a hypothetical normalized fourth-order AC state, average its four-copy projector over collective rotations:</p>'+m(r'X=\int_{\mathrm{SU}(2)} U_g^{\otimes4}(|\psi\rangle\langle\psi|)^{\otimes4}U_g^{\dagger\otimes4}\,dg,\qquad X\succeq0,\quad\operatorname{Tr}X=1.')+'<p>Its support lies in '+m(r'\operatorname{Sym}^4(V_{15/2})',False)+', of dimension 3876. The vanishing multipoles imply</p>'+m(r'\operatorname{Tr}_1[(T_{\ell0}\otimes I^{\otimes3})X]=0,\qquad\ell=1,2,3,4.')+'<p>The certificate uses 525 necessary equations on 579 real invariant coordinates. They are reconstructed directly in the physical tensor-word basis.</p></div>'
 b+='<div class="proof-step"><h3>2. Use positivity of the partial transpose</h3><p>The moment is a mixture of product projectors across the first copy and the other three copies, so '+m(r'X^{\Gamma_1}\succeq0',False)+'. Conjugating the transposed first factor by the spin-flip unitary gives a rotation-invariant operator '+m(r'Y\succeq0',False)+' on '+m(r'V_{15/2}\otimes\operatorname{Sym}^3(V_{15/2})',False)+', of dimension 13056.</p><p>The complete spin decompositions give 29 positive input coefficient matrices, with the certificate’s dyadic rescaling, '+m(r'B_J',False)+' and 31 positive matrix compressions '+m(r'Y_L',False)+'. The output blocks are exact linear functions of the input blocks. Taking real parts preserves both positivity conditions and the contraction equations, so arbitrary complex states are covered.</p></div>'
 b+='<div class="proof-step"><h3>3. A positive quantity would have to vanish</h3><p>A rational combination of the contraction equations gives the exact identity</p>'+m(r'0=\operatorname{Tr}X+\sum_J\operatorname{Tr}(C_JB_J)+\sum_L\operatorname{Tr}(Q_LY_L),\qquad C_J\succ0,\quad Q_L\succ0.')+'<p>Every summand after the trace is nonnegative, while '+m(r'\operatorname{Tr}X=1',False)+'. This is impossible. Exact rational LDL factorizations establish all 150 input and 522 output positivity pivots. Numerical optimization discovers the coefficients; the proof checks their rational identities and signs exactly.</p></div>'+links([('proof.tex','Complete LaTeX proof'),('certificate.json','Exact rational certificate'),('verify_independently.py','Independent physical-map verifier'),('independent-verification.json','Successful independent verification')])+'</section>'
 b+='<section><h2>Order three is attained</h2>'+m(r'|\psi\rangle=\frac{3(|D_{15}^{(0)}\rangle+|D_{15}^{(15)}\rangle)+\sqrt{35}(|D_{15}^{(4)}\rangle+|D_{15}^{(11)}\rangle)}{\sqrt{88}}.')+'<p>Support gaps eliminate off-diagonal spin moments through rank three. Reflection symmetry cancels the odd moments, and '+m(r'\langle J_z^2\rangle=85/4=j(j+1)/3',False)+'. This state therefore has globally maximum AC order three.</p>'+links([('../../index.html#n=15&t=3&subspace=sparse-third-n15','Dicke coefficients and Majorana representation'),('../../../anticoherent-state-catalogue/index.html#n=15&t=4','Matching pure-state catalogue exclusion')])+'</section>'
 b+='<section><h2>Reproducible verification</h2><p>The independent verifier reconstructs the representations, contraction equations and partial-transpose map, and checks the rational positive-definite certificate. The sign conventions were also tested on arbitrary complex product states and a known fourth-order state at seventeen qubits.</p><pre><code>python3 verify_independently.py</code></pre></section>'
 head='<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>N=15: fourth-order anticoherence is impossible</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.css"><script defer src="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.js"></script><style>'+css+'</style><script>document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded",()=>document.querySelectorAll("[data-tex]").forEach(el=>{if(window.katex)el.innerHTML=katex.renderToString(el.dataset.tex,{displayMode:el.dataset.display==="true",throwOnError:false,strict:"ignore",trust:false});}));</script></head><body><main>'
 (HERE/'index.html').write_text(head+b+'</main></body></html>\n')
if __name__=='__main__':main()
